From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Tray icons in the desktop's tray (StatusNotifierItem).

Under Wayland, explorer showed the icons of Shell_NotifyIcon (UnrealGameSync, P4V) in a window
of its own: winewayland has no XEMBED to dock them into the desktop's tray, as winex11 does.

In explorer, when the session bus has an org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher (KDE Plasma, and the
trays of other desktops), winewayland's NotifyIcon makes every icon a StatusNotifierItem: a
connection of its own to the session bus, so that the tray drops the item when the icon is
deleted, with the icon's pixels, its tip as title and tooltip, and NIS_HIDDEN as Passive.
Activate, ContextMenu and SecondaryActivate reach the icon's window as the clicks of explorer's
own tray window do (with NIN_SELECT and WM_CONTEXTMENU for NOTIFYICON_VERSION and later);
Activate is followed by a double click, since most Windows programs open on one; the cursor is put
where the tray was clicked, where programs open their menu. A Wine thread
of explorer serves the connections. libdbus is loaded at run time; without it or without a
watcher, NotifyIcon returns -1 and explorer shows the icon itself as before.

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/Makefile.in b/dlls/winewayland.drv/Makefile.in
index afe7902..e6df653 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/Makefile.in
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 MODULE = winewayland.drv
 UNIXLIB = winewayland.so
-UNIX_CFLAGS = $(EGL_CFLAGS) $(WAYLAND_CLIENT_CFLAGS) $(WAYLAND_EGL_CFLAGS) $(XKBCOMMON_CFLAGS) $(XKBREGISTRY_CFLAGS)
+UNIX_CFLAGS = $(DBUS_CFLAGS) $(EGL_CFLAGS) $(WAYLAND_CLIENT_CFLAGS) $(WAYLAND_EGL_CFLAGS) $(XKBCOMMON_CFLAGS) $(XKBREGISTRY_CFLAGS)
 UNIX_LIBS = -lwin32u $(WAYLAND_CLIENT_LIBS) $(WAYLAND_EGL_LIBS) $(XKBCOMMON_LIBS) $(XKBREGISTRY_LIBS) $(PTHREAD_LIBS) -lm
 IMPORTS = user32 win32u
 
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	opengl.c \
 	pointer-constraints-unstable-v1.xml \
 	pointer-warp-v1.xml \
+	systray.c \
 	relative-pointer-unstable-v1.xml \
 	text-input-unstable-v3.xml \
 	viewporter.xml \
